  (47, 2, E'Sector Lead Perm', 7, E'Sector Lead – Delivery – Permanent\n\nPurpose Of The Role\n\nThe Sector Lead is responsible for driving delivery performance, consistency and capability across a defined market while maintaining strong personal delivery on key roles.\n\nSector Leads operate as the point of ownership for delivery within their sector, raising standards, improving conversion and ensuring consistent candidate quality across all live roles.\n\nRole Responsibilities\n\nSector Delivery Performanc\n• Drive delivery performance across the sector through standards, accountability and visibilit\n• Ensure strong pipeline coverage across all live role\n• Maintain oversight of delivery activity, pipeline and conversion\n\nDelivery Standards & Qualit\n• Set and maintain high standards of candidate quality and relevanc\n• Ensure consistent delivery processes are followed across the secto\n• Identify and address gaps in delivery performance\n\nDelivery Strategy & Suppor\n• Support consultants on complex or high-priority role\n• Provide guidance on delivery approach, candidate strategy and pipeline buil\n• Act as a go-to person for delivery challenges within the sector\n\nPipeline & Market Ownershi\n• Maintain visibility of candidate pipelines across the secto\n• Identify trends in candidate availability and market condition\n• Ensure pipelines are aligned to current and future demand\n\nCollaboration & Influenc\n• Work closely with consultants to align delivery to client requirement\n• Influence delivery approach to improve outcomes and conversio\n• Share best practice and raise capability across the sector\n\nWhat Success Looks Like – How The Role Is Measured\n\nSector Delivery Performanc\n• Strong and consistent candidate delivery across all live role\n• Improved conversion rates across the secto\n• Increased success rate on roles supported\n\nPipeline Strengt\n• Strong and visible pipeline coverage across the secto\n• Reduced delivery gaps and improved candidate flow\n\nImpact & Influenc\n• Positive impact on delivery outcomes across multiple consultant\n• Increased consistency and standards across the secto\n• Acting as a trusted point of expertise\n\nQuality & Standard\n• High and consistent standards of candidate qualit\n• Strong adherence to delivery processes\n\nCandidate Experienc\n• Consistent and professional candidate journey across the sector\n\nProfessional Standard\n• Accurate CRM usage and pipeline visibilit\n• Strong organisation and accountability\n\nBehaviours & Values Expected In This Role\n\nSector Leads are expected to demonstrate:\n\nSector Ownership – taking responsibility for delivery performance across the secto\nAccountability – driving activity, pipeline and standards across multiple role\nInfluence – improving delivery outcomes through guidance and suppor\nQuality Leadership – setting and maintaining high delivery standard\nConsistency – ensuring reliable and structured delivery performance\n\nThese behaviours form part of probation and promotion assessments.\n\nSector Leads are also expected to consistently demonstrate our 6 DNA values:\n\nDriven\nHow much do you want to achieve your goals?\n\nDisciplined\nConsistently performing the small actions required to achieve your goals.\n\nCompetitive\nSelf-motivated and driven to continually achieve your best.\n\nPositive\nMaintaining a solutions-focused attitude.\n\nResilient\nBouncing back quickly from setbacks.\n\nCommitted\nShowing dedication to achieving your goals and contributing to team success.\n\nAt Sector Lead level these values are demonstrated through ownership of sector performance, raising standards and influencing delivery outcomes across others.\n\n', E'2026-04-17T10:04:50.335298'),
  (48, 2, E'Sector Lead Contract', 8, E'Sector Lead – Delivery – Contract\n\nPurpose Of The Role\n\nThe Sector Lead is responsible for driving delivery performance, pipeline strength and contractor quality across a defined market while maintaining strong personal delivery on key contract roles.\n\nSector Leads operate as the point of ownership for contract delivery within their sector, improving conversion, strengthening pipelines and ensuring consistent contractor quality across all live roles.\n\nRole Responsibilities\n\nSector Delivery Performanc\n• Drive contract delivery performance across the secto\n• Ensure strong contractor pipeline coverage across all live role\n• Maintain oversight of delivery activity, pipeline and conversion\n\nDelivery Standards & Qualit\n• Set and maintain high standards of contractor quality and relevanc\n• Ensure consistent delivery processes are followe\n• Identify and address gaps in contract delivery performance\n\nDelivery Strategy & Suppor\n• Support consultants on complex or high-priority contract role\n• Provide guidance on contractor strategy, availability and rate\n• Act as a go-to person for delivery challenges\n\nPipeline & Market Ownershi\n• Maintain visibility of contractor pipelines across the secto\n• Identify trends in contractor availability and deman\n• Ensure pipelines are aligned to current and future contract needs\n\nCollaboration & Influenc\n• Work closely with consultants to align delivery to client requirement\n• Influence delivery approach to improve contract outcome\n• Share best practice and raise capability across the sector\n\nWhat Success Looks Like – How The Role Is Measured\n\nSector Delivery Performanc\n• Strong and consistent contractor delivery across all live role\n• Improved conversion rates across the secto\n• Increased success rate on contract roles\n\nPipeline Strengt\n• Strong and visible contractor pipeline coverag\n• Reduced delivery gaps and improved contractor flow\n\nImpact & Influenc\n• Positive impact on contract delivery outcomes across multiple consultant\n• Increased consistency and standards across the sector\n\nQuality & Standard\n• High and consistent standards of contractor qualit\n• Strong adherence to delivery processes\n\nCandidate Experienc\n• Consistent and professional contractor experience\n\nProfessional Standard\n• Accurate CRM and compliance record\n• Strong organisation and accountability\n\nBehaviours & Values Expected In This Role\n\nSector Leads are expected to demonstrate:\n\nSector Ownership – taking responsibility for contract delivery performanc\nAccountability – driving pipeline, activity and standard\nInfluence – improving delivery outcomes across the secto\nQuality Leadership – setting and maintaining high standard\nConsistency – ensuring reliable and structured delivery performance\n\nThese behaviours form part of probation and promotion assessments.\n\nSector Leads are also expected to consistently demonstrate our 6 DNA values:\n\nDriven\nHow much do you want to achieve your goals?\n\nDisciplined\nConsistently performing the small actions required to achieve your goals.\n\nCompetitive\nSelf-motivated and driven to continually achieve your best.\n\nPositive\nMaintaining a solutions-focused attitude.\n\nResilient\nBouncing back quickly from setbacks.\n\nCommitted\nShowing dedication to achieving your goals and contributing to team success.\n\nAt Sector Lead level these values are demonstrated through ownership of sector performance, raising standards and influencing contract delivery outcomes across others.\n\n', E'2026-04-17T10:04:50.335298'),
  (49, 2, E'Team Leader Perm', 9, E'Team Leader – Delivery – Permanent\n\nPurpose Of The Role\n\nThe Team Leader is responsible for the performance, development and day-to-day management of a team of delivery consultants while maintaining strong personal delivery on key roles.\n\nTeam Leaders are accountable for driving team performance through clear expectations, coaching, accountability and consistent delivery standards.\n\nRole Responsibilities\n\nTeam Performance & Managemen\n• Take ownership of team delivery performance across permanent role\n• Set clear expectations around activity, pipeline and delivery standard\n• Monitor team performance and address underperformance where required\n\nCoaching & Developmen\n• Provide regular coaching to improve delivery capability and outcome\n• Support individuals in improving candidate quality, conversion and process managemen\n• Identify development needs and provide ongoing feedback\n\nDelivery Standards & Accountabilit\n• Ensure consistent delivery standards are maintained across the tea\n• Hold individuals accountable to activity, pipeline and quality expectation\n• Address gaps in performance and delivery consistency\n\nDelivery Support & Escalatio\n• Support the team on complex or high-priority role\n• Act as an escalation point for delivery challenge\n• Provide guidance on delivery strategy and candidate approach\n\nPipeline & Performance Visibilit\n• Maintain visibility of team pipeline, activity and delivery performanc\n• Ensure accurate CRM usage and reporting across the tea\n• Identify risks and take action to maintain performance levels\n\nCollaboration & Alignmen\n• Work closely with consultants and leadership to align delivery to client need\n• Ensure effective communication across the tea\n• Contribute to overall business performance through delivery success\n\nWhat Success Looks Like – How The Role Is Measured\n\nTeam Performanc\n• Consistent delivery performance across the tea\n• Improved conversion rates and placement outcome\n• Strong and reliable pipeline coverage across roles\n\nIndividual Developmen\n• Improvement in individual consultant capability and performanc\n• Increased consistency in delivery standards across the tea\n• Effective management of underperformance\n\nDelivery Quality & Standard\n• High and consistent standards of candidate qualit\n• Strong adherence to recruitment processes\n\nImpact & Leadershi\n• Positive impact on team performance and outcome\n• Clear accountability and ownership within the tea\n• Acting as a strong role model for delivery standards\n\nCandidate Experienc\n• Consistent and professional candidate journey across the team\n\nProfessional Standard\n• Accurate CRM usage and reportin\n• Strong organisation, communication and accountability\n\nBehaviours & Values Expected In This Role\n\nTeam Leaders are expected to demonstrate:\n\nLeadership – setting clear expectations and driving team performanc\nAccountability – holding individuals responsible for delivery outcome\nCoaching – developing capability through regular feedback and suppor\nOwnership – taking responsibility for team performance and result\nConsistency – maintaining reliable standards across the team\n\nThese behaviours form part of probation and promotion assessments.\n\nTeam Leaders are also expected to consistently demonstrate our 6 DNA values:\n\nDriven\nHow much do you want to achieve your goals?\n\nDisciplined\nConsistently performing the small actions required to achieve your goals.\n\nCompetitive\nSelf-motivated and driven to continually achieve your best.\n\nPositive\nMaintaining a solutions-focused attitude.\n\nResilient\nBouncing back quickly from setbacks.\n\nCommitted\nShowing dedication to achieving your goals and contributing to team success.\n\nAt Team Leader level these values are demonstrated through leadership of others, accountability for team performance and consistent raising of standards.\n\n', E'2026-04-17T10:04:50.335298'),
