  (63, 1, E'Team Leader Contract', 9, E'\n\nTeam Leader – Contract\n\n\n\n\n\nPurpose Of The Role\n\n\n\nThe Team Leader is responsible for driving the performance, development and commercial success of a team operating within a contract recruitment market while maintaining strong personal contract billing performance.\n\n\n\nTeam Leaders lead by example by building strong contractor books, coaching consultants to improve performance and ensuring strong contractor pipeline, activity and revenue standards across the team.\n\n\n\n\n\nRole Responsibilities\n\n\n\nTeam Leadership & Performance\n\n• Lead, motivate and support a team of consultants operating within the contract market\n\n• Drive contractor activity standards, pipeline management and recruitment discipline across the team\n\n• Monitor team performance against revenue and activity expectations\n\n• Provide regular feedback, coaching and performance support\n\n\n\nConsultant Development\n\n• Support consultants in developing contract recruitment capability\n\n• Identify capability gaps and support improvement\n\n• Contribute to onboarding and training of new team members\n\n• Share contract market knowledge, best practice and recruitment techniques\n\n\n\nClient Development & Market Growth\n\n• Develop strong client relationships within the contract market\n\n• Support consultants with client development and deal strategy\n\n• Expand opportunities within existing accounts and generate new business\n\n\n\nContractor Network Development\n\n• Maintain strong contractor networks\n\n• Support consultants in developing contractor relationships\n\n• Maintain visibility of contractor availability and market trends\n\n\n\nRecruitment Delivery\n\n• Maintain strong personal contract revenue performance\n\n• Support consultants with complex contract recruitment processes\n\n• Ensure high-quality delivery across all client and contractor interactions\n\n\n\nOperational Standards\n\n• Maintain accurate CRM records and reporting\n\n• Ensure recruitment processes and compliance standards are followed\n\n• Maintain visibility of team contractor pipeline, activity and revenue performance\n\n\n\n\n\nWhat Success Looks Like – How The Role Is Measured\n\n\n\nFinancial Performance\n\n• Achieving or exceeding personal contract revenue targets\n\n• Contributing to the overall contract revenue performance of the team\n\n• Supporting consistent contractor GP generation across the team\n\n\n\nTeam Performance\n\n• Driving activity standards and recruitment discipline across the team\n\n• Supporting consultants to improve contract recruitment capability\n\n• Contributing to improved contract revenue performance\n\n\n\nPipeline & Business Development\n\n• Maintaining strong client relationships\n\n• Supporting consultants to develop contract client opportunities\n\n• Ensuring strong contractor pipeline visibility across the team\n\n\n\nCustomer Experience\n\n• Maintaining strong relationships with clients and contractors\n\n• Ensuring high-quality recruitment delivery across the team\n\n\n\nProfessional Standards\n\n• Maintaining accurate CRM records and reporting\n\n• Ensuring recruitment processes and compliance standards are followed\n\n• Operating with strong organisation, communication and professionalism\n\n\n\n\n\nBehaviours & Values Expected In This Role\n\n\n\nTeam Leaders are expected to demonstrate:\n\n\n\nLeadership & Accountability – taking responsibility for team performance as well as personal delivery\n\nCommercial Ownership – understanding and driving contract revenue performance across the team\n\nCoaching & Development – actively supporting consultants to improve capability and performance\n\nResilience – maintaining momentum through challenges and market fluctuations\n\nRole Modelling – consistently demonstrating the behaviours and standards expected across the team\n\n\n\nThese behaviours form part of probation and promotion assessments.\n\n\n\nTeam Leaders are also expected to consistently demonstrate our 6 DNA values:\n\n\n\nDriven  \n\nHow much do you want to achieve your goals?\n\n\n\nDisciplined  \n\nConsistently performing the small actions required to achieve your goals.\n\n\n\nCompetitive  \n\nSelf-motivated and driven to continually achieve your best.\n\n\n\nPositive  \n\nMaintaining a solutions-focused attitude.\n\n\n\nResilient  \n\nBouncing back quickly from setbacks.\n\n\n\nCommitted  \n\nShowing dedication to achieving your goals and contributing to team success.\n\n\n\nAt Team Leader level these values are demonstrated through leadership, accountability for team performance and supporting the development of others.\n\n\n\n\n\n', E'2026-04-17T10:04:54.088555'),
  (64, 1, E'Team Leader Perm', 10, E'\n\nTeam Leader – Permanent\n\n\n\n\n\nPurpose Of The Role\n\n\n\nThe Team Leader is responsible for driving the performance, development and commercial success of a team of recruitment consultants while maintaining strong personal billing performance.\n\n\n\nTeam Leaders lead by example through consistent delivery, coaching consultants to improve performance and ensuring strong activity, pipeline and revenue standards across the team.\n\n\n\n\n\nRole Responsibilities\n\n\n\nTeam Leadership & Performance\n\n• Lead, motivate and support a team of recruitment consultants\n\n• Drive activity standards, pipeline management and recruitment discipline across the team\n\n• Monitor team performance against revenue and activity expectations\n\n• Provide regular feedback, coaching and performance support\n\n\n\nConsultant Development\n\n• Support the development of consultants through coaching and guidance\n\n• Identify capability gaps and support improvement\n\n• Contribute to onboarding and training of new team members\n\n• Share market knowledge, best practice and recruitment techniques\n\n\n\nClient Development & Market Growth\n\n• Develop strong client relationships within your market\n\n• Support consultants with client development and deal strategy\n\n• Expand opportunities within existing accounts and generate new business\n\n\n\nRecruitment Delivery\n\n• Maintain strong personal billing performance\n\n• Support consultants with complex recruitment processes\n\n• Ensure high-quality delivery across all client and candidate interactions\n\n\n\nOperational Standards\n\n• Maintain accurate CRM records and reporting\n\n• Ensure recruitment processes and compliance standards are followed\n\n• Maintain visibility of team pipeline, activity and revenue performance\n\n\n\n\n\nWhat Success Looks Like – How The Role Is Measured\n\n\n\nFinancial Performance\n\n• Achieving or exceeding personal revenue targets\n\n• Contributing to the overall revenue performance of the team\n\n• Supporting consistent billing performance across the team\n\n\n\nTeam Performance\n\n• Driving activity standards and recruitment discipline across the team\n\n• Supporting consultants to improve capability and performance\n\n• Contributing to improved team revenue performance\n\n\n\nPipeline & Business Development\n\n• Maintaining strong client relationships\n\n• Supporting consultants to develop client opportunities\n\n• Ensuring strong pipeline visibility across the team\n\n\n\nCustomer Experience\n\n• Maintaining strong relationships with clients and candidates\n\n• Ensuring high-quality recruitment delivery across the team\n\n\n\nProfessional Standards\n\n• Maintaining accurate CRM records and reporting\n\n• Ensuring recruitment processes and compliance standards are followed\n\n• Operating with strong organisation, communication and professionalism\n\n\n\n\n\nBehaviours & Values Expected In This Role\n\n\n\nTeam Leaders are expected to demonstrate:\n\n\n\nLeadership & Accountability – taking responsibility for team performance as well as personal delivery\n\nCommercial Ownership – understanding and driving revenue performance across the team\n\nCoaching & Development – actively supporting consultants to improve capability and performance\n\nResilience – maintaining momentum through challenges and market fluctuations\n\nRole Modelling – consistently demonstrating the behaviours and standards expected across the team\n\n\n\nThese behaviours form part of probation and promotion assessments.\n\n\n\nTeam Leaders are also expected to consistently demonstrate our 6 DNA values:\n\n\n\nDriven  \n\nHow much do you want to achieve your goals?\n\n\n\nDisciplined  \n\nConsistently performing the small actions required to achieve your goals.\n\n\n\nCompetitive  \n\nSelf-motivated and driven to continually achieve your best.\n\n\n\nPositive  \n\nMaintaining a solutions-focused attitude.\n\n\n\nResilient  \n\nBouncing back quickly from setbacks.\n\n\n\nCommitted  \n\nShowing dedication to achieving your goals and contributing to team success.\n\n\n\nAt Team Leader level these values are demonstrated through leadership, accountability for team performance and supporting the development of others.\n\n\n\n\n\n', E'2026-04-17T10:04:54.088555'),
  (65, 1, E'Divisional Manager Contract', 11, E'\n\nDivisional Manager – Contract\n\n\n\n\n\nPurpose Of The Role\n\n\n\nThe Divisional Manager is responsible for the commercial performance, growth and leadership of a contract recruitment division.\n\n\n\nDivisional Managers are accountable for the overall contract revenue performance of the division, driving team output, contractor pipeline strength and consistent commercial delivery across multiple teams or sectors.\n\n\n\n\n\nRole Responsibilities\n\n\n\nDivision Leadership & Performance\n\n• Lead and develop Team Leaders, Sector Leads and Consultants within the contract division  \n\n• Drive contractor revenue performance across the division  \n\n• Monitor and manage performance against divisional targets  \n\n• Set clear expectations around activity, pipeline and delivery standards  \n\n\n\nCommercial Strategy & Growth\n\n• Define and execute the contract strategy for the division  \n\n• Identify growth opportunities across clients, sectors and contractor markets  \n\n• Ensure strong contractor pipeline and revenue forecasting  \n\n• Drive expansion within key accounts  \n\n\n\nPeople Leadership & Development\n\n• Develop leadership capability within Team Leaders and Sector Leads  \n\n• Support performance management and capability development  \n\n• Build a high-performance culture focused on accountability and delivery  \n\n\n\nClient Development\n\n• Develop strategic relationships with key contract clients  \n\n• Support teams on complex deals and high-value accounts  \n\n• Position the business as a specialist contract partner  \n\n\n\nOperational Standards\n\n• Maintain visibility of contractor pipelines, activity and performance  \n\n• Ensure compliance and contractor processes are followed  \n\n• Maintain accurate reporting and forecasting across the division  \n\n\n\n\n\nWhat Success Looks Like – How The Role Is Measured\n\n\n\nFinancial Performance\n\n• Achieving or exceeding divisional contract revenue targets  \n\n• Driving consistent contractor GP performance across teams  \n\n• Delivering sustainable revenue growth  \n\n\n\nDivision Growth\n\n• Expanding client relationships and contractor opportunities  \n\n• Building scalable contractor pipelines  \n\n• Identifying new contract revenue streams  \n\n\n\nLeadership & Team Performance\n\n• Improving performance and capability across teams  \n\n• Developing future leaders within the division  \n\n• Driving consistent activity and delivery standards  \n\n\n\nCustomer Experience\n\n• Maintaining strong strategic client relationships  \n\n• Ensuring high-quality contract recruitment delivery  \n\n\n\nProfessional Standards\n\n• Maintaining accurate reporting and forecasting  \n\n• Ensuring compliance and operational standards are met  \n\n\n\n\n\nBehaviours & Values Expected In This Role\n\n\n\nStrategic Leadership – driving direction and performance across the division\n\nCommercial Ownership – full accountability for divisional contract revenue\n\nLeadership Development – developing leaders within the business\n\nInfluence – aligning teams to standards and expectations\n\nRole Modelling – setting behavioural and performance standards\n\n\n\nDivisional Managers are also expected to consistently demonstrate our 6 DNA values:\n\n\n\nDriven  \n\nHow much do you want to achieve your goals?\n\n\n\n\n\nDisciplined  \n\nConsistently performing the small actions required to achieve your goals.\n\n\n\nCompetitive  \n\nSelf-motivated and driven to continually achieve your best.\n\n\n\nPositive  \n\nMaintaining a solutions-focused attitude.\n\n\n\nResilient  \n\nBouncing back quickly from setbacks.\n\n\n\nCommitted  \n\nShowing dedication to achieving your goals and contributing to team success.\n\n\n\nAt Divisional Manager level these values are demonstrated through leadership, strategic thinking and accountability for the success of the wider division.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n', E'2026-04-17T10:04:54.088555'),
  (66, 1, E'Divisional Manager Perm', 12, E'\n\nDivisional Manager – Permanent\n\n\n\n\n\nPurpose Of The Role\n\n\n\nThe Divisional Manager is responsible for the commercial performance, growth and leadership of a defined recruitment division.\n\n\n\nDivisional Managers drive revenue performance through strong leadership, strategic client development and the development of high-performing recruitment teams.\n\n\n\n\n\nRole Responsibilities\n\n\n\nDivision Leadership & Performance\n\n• Lead and develop a team of consultants, team leaders and sector leads\n\n• Drive revenue, activity and performance standards across the division\n\n• Monitor division performance against revenue targets and growth plans\n\n• Provide leadership, direction and accountability for team performance\n\n\n\nCommercial Strategy & Growth\n\n• Develop and execute the commercial strategy for the division\n\n• Identify growth opportunities within existing client accounts and new markets\n\n• Support senior consultants and leaders in developing strategic client relationships\n\n• Ensure strong pipeline visibility and revenue forecasting across the division\n\n\n\nPeople Leadership & Development\n\n• Recruit, develop and retain high-performing consultants and leaders\n\n• Support leadership capability within team leaders and sector leads\n\n• Provide coaching, guidance and performance management where required\n\n• Build a high-performance culture within the division\n\n\n\nClient Development\n\n• Develop and maintain strategic relationships with key clients\n\n• Support teams with complex recruitment processes and major accounts\n\n• Position the business as a specialist partner within the market\n\n\n\nOperational Standards\n\n• Maintain accurate reporting across the division\n\n• Ensure recruitment processes, compliance and operational standards are followed\n\n• Maintain visibility of pipeline, activity and performance metrics across the division\n\n\n\n\n\nWhat Success Looks Like – How The Role Is Measured\n\n\n\nFinancial Performance\n\n• Achieving or exceeding divisional revenue targets\n\n• Delivering consistent revenue growth across the division\n\n• Supporting strong billing performance across consultants and teams\n\n\n\nDivision Growth\n\n• Expanding client relationships and market presence\n\n• Building a sustainable pipeline of opportunities across the division\n\n• Developing new revenue streams or sectors where appropriate\n\n\n\nLeadership & Team Performance\n\n• Developing high-performing consultants and team leaders\n\n• Supporting progression and promotion across the division\n\n• Building a strong performance culture and accountability\n\n\n\nCustomer Experience\n\n• Maintaining strong strategic relationships with key clients\n\n• Ensuring high-quality recruitment delivery across the division\n\n\n\nProfessional Standards\n\n• Maintaining accurate reporting and forecasting\n\n• Ensuring compliance and recruitment standards are consistently followed\n\n• Operating with strong organisation, leadership and communication\n\n\n\n\n\nBehaviours & Values Expected In This Role\n\n\n\nDivisional Managers are expected to demonstrate:\n\n\n\nStrategic Leadership – setting direction and driving performance across the division\n\nCommercial Ownership – full accountability for divisional revenue and growth\n\nLeadership Development – developing future leaders within the business\n\nResilience – maintaining performance through market challenges\n\nRole Modelling – consistently demonstrating the behaviours and standards expected across the business\n\n\n\nThese behaviours form part of probation and promotion assessments.\n\n\n\nDivisional Managers are also expected to consistently demonstrate our 6 DNA values:\n\n\n\nDriven  \n\nHow much do you want to achieve your goals?\n\n\n\nDisciplined  \n\nConsistently performing the small actions required to achieve your goals.\n\n\n\nCompetitive  \n\nSelf-motivated and driven to continually achieve your best.\n\n\n\nPositive  \n\nMaintaining a solutions-focused attitude.\n\n\n\nResilient  \n\nBouncing back quickly from setbacks.\n\n\n\nCommitted  \n\nShowing dedication to achieving your goals and contributing to team success.\n\n\n\nAt Divisional Manager level these values are demonstrated through leadership, strategic thinking and accountability for the success of the wider division.\n\n\n\n\n\n', E'2026-04-17T10:04:54.088555'),
  (67, 1, E'Associate Director Contract', 13, E'\n\nAssociate Director – Contract\n\n\n\n\n\nPurpose Of The Role\n\n\n\nThe Associate Director is responsible for the commercial performance, growth and strategic direction of a contract recruitment business area.\n\n\n\nAssociate Directors drive contract revenue growth across multiple teams or divisions, shaping strategy, influencing leadership performance and contributing to the overall direction of the business.\n\n\n\n\n\nRole Responsibilities\n\n\n\nBusiness Leadership & Strategy\n\n• Define and execute the contract strategy across your area of the business  \n\n• Identify growth opportunities across markets, clients and contractor pipelines  \n\n• Contribute to business-wide planning and strategic decisions  \n\n• Align division performance with overall business objectives  \n\n\n\nCommercial Performance & Growth\n\n• Drive contract revenue growth across multiple divisions or sectors  \n\n• Ensure strong contractor pipeline visibility and forecasting  \n\n• Identify and unlock new revenue opportunities  \n\n• Support leaders in delivering sustainable performance  \n\n\n\nLeadership & Influence\n\n• Influence Divisional Managers and senior leaders  \n\n• Drive performance standards, accountability and consistency  \n\n• Act as a senior escalation point for complex commercial situations  \n\n• Shape leadership behaviours across the business  \n\n\n\nClient & Market Leadership\n\n• Develop relationships with key strategic contract clients  \n\n• Support major deals and complex contractor engagements  \n\n• Position the business as a market leader  \n\n• Provide insight into contractor trends and opportunities  \n\n\n\nOperational & Commercial Governance\n\n• Maintain oversight of performance, reporting and forecasting  \n\n• Ensure alignment between commercial activity and business strategy  \n\n• Ensure contractor compliance standards are maintained  \n\n\n\n\n\nWhat Success Looks Like – How The Role Is Measured\n\n\n\nBusiness Performance\n\n• Achieving or exceeding contract revenue targets across your area  \n\n• Delivering consistent and sustainable revenue growth  \n\n• Expanding contractor pipelines and client relationships  \n\n\n\nStrategic Impact\n\n• Driving growth initiatives and market expansion  \n\n• Contributing to business direction and strategy  \n\n• Improving performance structures and commercial approach  \n\n\n\nLeadership & Influence\n\n• Supporting and influencing leaders to improve performance  \n\n• Raising standards across divisions  \n\n• Developing leadership capability within the business  \n\n\n\nCustomer Experience\n\n• Building strong strategic client relationships  \n\n• Supporting high-quality contract delivery  \n\n\n\nProfessional Standards\n\n• Maintaining strong commercial oversight and reporting  \n\n• Ensuring compliance and operational excellence  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBehaviours & Values Expected In This Role\n\nAssociate Directors are expected to demonstrate:\n\n\n\nStrategic Leadership – shaping direction and driving performance across the business\n\nCommercial Ownership – accountability for revenue growth and business performance\n\nInfluence & Alignment – aligning leaders and teams to business objectives\n\nResilience – maintaining performance through change and market challenges\n\nRole Modelling – setting behavioural and professional standards across the organisation\n\n\n\nThese behaviours form part of probation and promotion assessments.\n\n\n\nAssociate Directors are also expected to consistently demonstrate our 6 DNA values:\n\n\n\nDriven  \n\nHow much do you want to achieve your goals?\n\n\n\nDisciplined  \n\nConsistently performing the small actions required to achieve your goals.\n\n\n\nCompetitive  \n\nSelf-motivated and driven to continually achieve your best.\n\n\n\nPositive  \n\nMaintaining a solutions-focused attitude.\n\n\n\nResilient  \n\nBouncing back quickly from setbacks.\n\n\n\nCommitted  \n\nShowing dedication to achieving your goals and contributing to team success.\n\n\n\nAt Associate Director level these values are demonstrated through strategic leadership, commercial ownership and influencing standards across the business.\n\n\n\n\n\n', E'2026-04-17T10:04:54.088555'),
  (68, 1, E'Associate Director Perm', 14, E'\n\nAssociate Director – Permanent\n\n\n\n\n\nPurpose Of The Role\n\n\n\nThe Associate Director is responsible for the commercial performance, growth and strategic direction of a defined area of the business.\n\n\n\nAssociate Directors operate as senior leaders within the organisation, driving revenue growth, developing market strategy and influencing performance across multiple teams or sectors.\n\n\n\nThey contribute to business-wide decision making and play a key role in shaping the direction, standards and long-term success of the organisation.\n\n\n\n\n\nRole Responsibilities\n\n\n\nBusiness Leadership & Strategy\n\n• Define and execute the commercial strategy for your area of the business\n\n• Identify opportunities for growth across markets, clients and sectors\n\n• Contribute to wider business planning and strategic decision making\n\n• Align team and sector performance with overall business objectives\n\n\n\nCommercial Performance & Growth\n\n• Drive revenue growth across multiple teams or sectors\n\n• Ensure strong pipeline visibility and forecasting across your area\n\n• Identify and unlock new revenue opportunities\n\n• Support leaders to deliver consistent and sustainable performance\n\n\n\nLeadership & Influence\n\n• Influence and support Divisional Managers, Team Leaders and Sector Leads\n\n• Drive high performance standards through clarity, accountability and expectation setting\n\n• Act as a senior escalation point for complex commercial or client situations\n\n• Shape leadership behaviours and standards across the business\n\n\n\nClient & Market Leadership\n\n• Develop and maintain relationships with key strategic clients\n\n• Position the business as a leading specialist within target markets\n\n• Support major deals, strategic accounts and complex negotiations\n\n• Provide insight into market trends and opportunities\n\n\n\nOperational & Commercial Governance\n\n• Ensure consistent reporting, forecasting and performance tracking\n\n• Maintain oversight of recruitment standards, processes and compliance\n\n• Ensure alignment between commercial activity and business objectives\n\n\n\n\n\nWhat Success Looks Like – How The Role Is Measured\n\n\n\nBusiness Performance\n\n• Achieving or exceeding revenue targets across your area of the business\n\n• Delivering consistent and sustainable revenue growth\n\n• Expanding market presence and client relationships\n\n\n\nStrategic Impact\n\n• Identifying and executing growth opportunities\n\n• Contributing to business strategy and decision making\n\n• Driving improvements in performance, structure and approach\n\n\n\nLeadership & Influence\n\n• Supporting and influencing leaders to improve performance\n\n• Raising standards and consistency across teams or sectors\n\n• Contributing to the development of future leaders\n\n\n\nCustomer Experience\n\n• Building strong strategic client relationships\n\n• Supporting delivery of high-quality recruitment solutions\n\n\n\nProfessional Standards\n\n• Maintaining strong oversight of performance, reporting and forecasting\n\n• Operating with high levels of organisation, communication and accountability\n\n\n\n\n\nBehaviours & Values Expected In This Role\n\n\n\nAssociate Directors are expected to demonstrate:\n\n\n\nStrategic Leadership – shaping direction and driving performance across the business\n\nCommercial Ownership – accountability for revenue growth and business performance\n\nInfluence & Alignment – aligning leaders and teams to business objectives\n\nResilience – maintaining performance through change and market challenges\n\nRole Modelling – setting behavioural and professional standards across the organisation\n\n\n\nThese behaviours form part of probation and promotion assessments.\n\n\n\nAssociate Directors are also expected to consistently demonstrate our 6 DNA values:\n\n\n\nDriven  \n\nHow much do you want to achieve your goals?\n\n\n\nDisciplined  \n\nConsistently performing the small actions required to achieve your goals.\n\n\n\nCompetitive  \n\nSelf-motivated and driven to continually achieve your best.\n\n\n\nPositive  \n\nMaintaining a solutions-focused attitude.\n\n\n\nResilient  \n\nBouncing back quickly from setbacks.\n\n\n\nCommitted  \n\nShowing dedication to achieving your goals and contributing to team success.\n\n\n\nAt Associate Director level these values are demonstrated through strategic leadership, commercial ownership and influencing standards across the business.\n\n\n\n\n\n', E'2026-04-17T10:04:54.088555'),
  (41, 2, E'Recruitment Consultant Perm', 1, E'\n\nDelivery Consultant – Permanent\n\n\n\n\n\nPurpose Of The Role\n\n\n\nThe Delivery Consultant is responsible for managing candidate pipelines and delivering high-quality candidates into permanent recruitment processes.\n\n\n\nDelivery Consultants take ownership of the delivery side of recruitment, ensuring roles are supported with relevant, qualified candidates and contributing directly to successful placements.\n\n\n\n\n\nRole Responsibilities\n\n\n\nCandidate Delivery & Ownership\n\n• Take ownership of candidate delivery across assigned permanent roles  \n\n• Build and manage candidate pipelines aligned to client requirements  \n\n• Ensure a consistent flow of relevant candidates into live processes  \n\n\n\nCandidate Qualification\n\n• Conduct detailed qualification calls to assess suitability  \n\n• Evaluate experience, motivations and long-term fit  \n\n• Ensure high standards of candidate quality before submission  \n\n\n\nProcess Management\n\n• Manage candidates through the recruitment process from submission to offer  \n\n• Coordinate interviews and maintain candidate engagement  \n\n• Identify and manage risks within the process (drop-offs, counteroffers, delays)  \n\n\n\nPipeline Management\n\n• Build and maintain structured pipelines across roles and markets  \n\n• Ensure sufficient candidate coverage for all live roles  \n\n• Proactively identify and address pipeline gaps  \n\n\n\nCollaboration\n\n• Work closely with 360 consultants to understand role requirements  \n\n• Align delivery approach to client expectations  \n\n• Contribute to successful placement outcomes  \n\n\n\n\n\nWhat Success Looks Like – How The Role Is Measured\n\n\n\nDelivery Performance\n\n• Consistently supporting roles with qualified candidates  \n\n• Contributing to successful placements through effective delivery  \n\n• Maintaining strong pipeline coverage across live roles  \n\n\n\nConversion & Quality\n\n• Achieving strong CV to interview conversion rates  \n\n• Supporting interview to placement conversion  \n\n• Delivering consistently relevant and well-qualified candidates  \n\n\n\nSpeed & Efficiency\n\n• Delivering candidates within required timeframes  \n\n• Maintaining momentum across recruitment processes  \n\n• Managing multiple roles effectively  \n\n\n\nActivity & Pipeline\n\n• Maintaining consistent sourcing and candidate engagement activity  \n\n• Building and managing structured candidate pipelines  \n\n\n\nCandidate Experience\n\n• Providing a professional and consistent candidate journey  \n\n• Managing expectations and communication effectively  \n\n\n\nProfessional Standards\n\n• Maintaining accurate CRM records  \n\n• Following recruitment processes and standards  \n\n• Operating with organisation and accountability  \n\n\n\n\n\nBehaviours & Values Expected In This Role\n\n\n\nDelivery Consultants are expected to demonstrate:\n\n\n\nOwnership – taking responsibility for delivery outcomes\n\nAccountability – owning activity levels and pipeline performance\n\nQuality Focus – prioritising relevance and standard of candidates\n\nConsistency – maintaining reliable delivery output\n\nCollaboration – working effectively with consultants and teams\n\n\n\nDelivery Consultants are also expected to consistently demonstrate our 6 DNA values:\n\n\n\nDriven  \n\nHow much do you want to achieve your goals?\n\n\n\nDisciplined  \n\nConsistently performing the small actions required to achieve your goals.\n\n\n\nCompetitive  \n\nSelf-motivated and driven to continually achieve your best.\n\n\n\nPositive  \n\nMaintaining a solutions-focused attitude.\n\n\n\nResilient  \n\nBouncing back quickly from setbacks.\n\n\n\nCommitted  \n\nShowing dedication to achieving your goals and contributing to team success.\n\n\n\n\n\nAt Delivery Consultant level these values are demonstrated through ownership of delivery, consistency of performance and contribution to placement outcomes.\n\n\n\n\n\n', E'2026-04-17T10:04:50.335298'),
  (42, 2, E'Recruitment Consultant Contract', 2, E'\n\nDelivery Consultant – Contract\n\n\n\n\n\nPurpose Of The Role\n\n\n\nThe Delivery Consultant is responsible for managing contractor pipelines and delivering high-quality contractors into live recruitment processes.\n\n\n\nDelivery Consultants take ownership of contract delivery, ensuring roles are supported with relevant contractors and contributing directly to contract revenue through effective pipeline management and candidate engagement.\n\n\n\n\n\nRole Responsibilities\n\n\n\nContractor Delivery & Ownership\n\n• Take ownership of contractor delivery across assigned roles  \n\n• Build and manage contractor pipelines aligned to role requirements  \n\n• Ensure a consistent flow of relevant contractors into live processes  \n\n\n\nContractor Qualification\n\n• Conduct detailed qualification of contractors  \n\n• Assess experience, availability, rate expectations and suitability  \n\n• Ensure high-quality contractor submissions  \n\n\n\nProcess Management\n\n• Manage contractors through the recruitment process from submission to onboarding  \n\n• Coordinate interviews and maintain contractor engagement  \n\n• Identify and manage risks within the process (drop-offs, availability changes, rate challenges)  \n\n\n\nPipeline Management\n\n• Build and maintain structured contractor pipelines across roles and markets  \n\n• Ensure strong contractor coverage for live roles  \n\n• Proactively identify and address pipeline gaps  \n\n\n\nCollaboration\n\n• Work closely with consultants to understand contract requirements  \n\n• Align delivery approach to client expectations  \n\n• Contribute to successful contractor placements  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWhat Success Looks Like – How The Role Is Measured\n\n\n\nDelivery Performance\n\n• Consistently delivering relevant contractors into live roles  \n\n• Supporting contract placements through effective delivery  \n\n• Maintaining strong contractor pipeline coverage  \n\n\n\nConversion & Quality\n\n• Achieving strong CV to interview conversion rates  \n\n• Supporting interview to placement conversion  \n\n• Delivering consistently relevant and well-qualified contractors  \n\n\n\nSpeed & Efficiency\n\n• Delivering contractors within required timeframes  \n\n• Maintaining momentum across contract processes  \n\n• Managing multiple roles effectively  \n\n\n\nActivity & Pipeline\n\n• Maintaining consistent sourcing and engagement activity  \n\n• Building structured contractor pipelines  \n\n\n\nCandidate Experience\n\n• Providing a professional contractor experience  \n\n• Managing expectations and communication effectively  \n\n\n\nProfessional Standards\n\n• Maintaining accurate CRM and compliance records  \n\n• Following contract recruitment processes  \n\n• Operating with organisation and accountability  \n\n\n\n\n\nBehaviours & Values Expected In This Role\n\n\n\nDelivery Consultants are expected to demonstrate:\n\n\n\nOwnership – taking responsibility for delivery outcomes\n\nAccountability – owning pipeline and performance\n\nQuality Focus – ensuring strong contractor suitability\n\nConsistency – maintaining reliable delivery output\n\nCollaboration – working effectively with consultants and teams\n\n\n\n\n\nDelivery Consultants are also expected to consistently demonstrate our 6 DNA values:\n\n\n\nDriven  \n\nHow much do you want to achieve your goals?\n\n\n\nDisciplined  \n\nConsistently performing the small actions required to achieve your goals.\n\n\n\nCompetitive  \n\nSelf-motivated and driven to continually achieve your best.\n\n\n\nPositive  \n\nMaintaining a solutions-focused attitude.\n\n\n\nResilient  \n\nBouncing back quickly from setbacks.\n\n\n\nCommitted  \n\nShowing dedication to achieving your goals and contributing to team success.\n\n\n\n\n\nAt Delivery Consultant level these values are demonstrated through ownership of delivery, consistency of performance and contribution to contract outcomes.\n\n\n\n\n\n', E'2026-04-17T10:04:50.335298'),
