  (51, 2, E'Divisional Manager Perm', 11, E'Divisional Manager Delivery – Permanent\n\nPurpose Of The Role\n\nThe Divisional Manager is responsible for the overall performance, structure and output of a delivery division, ensuring consistent candidate delivery, strong conversion and high-quality recruitment outcomes across the business.\n\nDivisional Managers lead through direction, structure and accountability, creating an environment where delivery teams perform consistently and at scale.\n\nRole Responsibilities\n\nDivision Performance & Ownershi\n• Take ownership of delivery performance across the divisio\n• Drive consistent candidate delivery, conversion and placement outcome\n• Ensure the division meets performance expectations and business objectives\n\nLeadership & Directio\n• Set clear direction, priorities and expectations across delivery team\n• Ensure Team Leaders are effectively managing and developing their team\n• Provide guidance and support to leadership within the division\n\nPerformance Managemen\n• Monitor divisional performance across activity, pipeline, conversion and outpu\n• Identify risks, gaps and areas for improvemen\n• Take action to improve performance across teams\n\nCapability & Standard\n• Ensure consistent delivery standards across the divisio\n• Drive improvements in candidate quality, pipeline management and proces\n• Raise capability through structure, coaching frameworks and leadership alignment\n\nPipeline & Forecastin\n• Maintain visibility of divisional pipeline and delivery performanc\n• Ensure pipelines are aligned to current and future deman\n• Support forecasting of delivery output and placement outcomes\n\nCollaboration & Business Alignmen\n• Work closely with senior leadership and consultants to align delivery to client need\n• Ensure delivery function supports overall business growth and performanc\n• Contribute to wider strategic decisions impacting delivery\n\n\n\nWhat Success Looks Like – How The Role Is Measured\n\nDivisional Performanc\n• Consistent delivery performance across all team\n• Strong conversion rates and placement outcome\n• Delivery function contributing to overall business success\n\nLeadership Impac\n• Effective leadership of Team Leaders and delivery team\n• Strong accountability and ownership across the divisio\n• Consistent standards and performance across teams\n\nPipeline & Forecastin\n• Strong and visible pipeline coverage across the divisio\n• Improved forecasting accuracy and delivery predictability\n\nCapability & Standard\n• Increased consistency in candidate quality and delivery processe\n• Improvement in team capability and performance\n\nCustomer Experienc\n• High-quality candidate experience across the divisio\n• Consistent delivery standards across all interactions\n\nProfessional Standard\n• Accurate CRM usage and reporting across team\n• Strong organisation, communication and accountability\n\nBehaviours & Values Expected In This Role\n\nDivisional Managers are expected to demonstrate:\n\nStrategic Ownership – taking responsibility for divisional performance and outcome\nLeadership – setting direction and enabling leaders to perfor\nAccountability – holding leaders and teams responsible for performanc\nCommercial Awareness – understanding how delivery impacts business performanc\nConsistency – ensuring reliable standards across the division\n\nThese behaviours form part of probation and promotion assessments.\n\nDivisional Managers are also expected to consistently demonstrate our 6 DNA values:\n\nDriven\nHow much do you want to achieve your goals?\n\nDisciplined\nConsistently performing the small actions required to achieve your goals.\n\nCompetitive\nSelf-motivated and driven to continually achieve your best.\n\nPositive\nMaintaining a solutions-focused attitude.\n\nResilient\nBouncing back quickly from setbacks.\n\nCommitted\nShowing dedication to achieving your goals and contributing to team success.\n\nAt Divisional Manager level these values are demonstrated through leadership at scale, ownership of performance and consistent delivery of results across multiple teams.\n\n', E'2026-04-17T10:04:50.335298'),
  (52, 2, E'Divisional Manager Contract', 12, E'Divisional Manager Delivery – Contract\n\nPurpose Of The Role\n\nThe Divisional Manager is responsible for the overall performance, pipeline strength and contractor delivery output across a contract delivery division.\n\nDivisional Managers lead the contract delivery function through direction, structure and accountability, ensuring consistent contractor pipelines, strong conversion and reliable contract revenue generation.\n\nRole Responsibilities\n\nDivision Performance & Ownershi\n• Take ownership of contract delivery performance across the divisio\n• Drive consistent contractor pipelines, conversion and placement outcome\n• Ensure delivery function supports contract revenue growth\n\nLeadership & Directio\n• Set clear expectations and priorities across delivery team\n• Ensure Team Leaders are effectively managing contract delivery performanc\n• Provide guidance and support to leadership within the division\n\nPerformance Managemen\n• Monitor divisional performance across pipeline, activity and conversio\n• Identify risks including pipeline gaps and contractor availabilit\n• Take action to improve performance across teams\n\nCapability & Standard\n• Ensure consistent contract delivery standards across the divisio\n• Drive improvements in contractor quality, pipeline management and complianc\n• Raise capability through structure and leadership alignment\n\nPipeline & Forecastin\n• Maintain visibility of contractor pipelines across the divisio\n• Ensure pipelines are aligned to current and future contract deman\n• Support forecasting of contractor placements and revenue\n\nCollaboration & Business Alignmen\n• Work closely with senior leadership and consultant\n• Ensure delivery function supports overall contract strateg\n• Contribute to wider strategic decisions impacting delivery\n\n\n\nWhat Success Looks Like – How The Role Is Measured\n\nDivisional Performanc\n• Consistent contract delivery performance across team\n• Strong conversion rates and contractor placement outcome\n• Contribution to contract revenue growth\n\nLeadership Impac\n• Effective leadership of Team Leaders and delivery team\n• Strong accountability across the division\n\nPipeline & Forecastin\n• Strong contractor pipeline coverage across the divisio\n• Improved forecasting accuracy\n\nCapability & Standard\n• Increased consistency in contractor quality and delivery processe\n• Improvement in team capability and performance\n\nCustomer Experienc\n• High-quality contractor experience across the division\n\nProfessional Standard\n• Accurate CRM and compliance reportin\n• Strong organisation and accountability\n\nBehaviours & Values Expected In This Role\n\nDivisional Managers are expected to demonstrate:\n\nStrategic Ownership – taking responsibility for divisional contract performanc\nLeadership – setting direction and enabling leaders to perfor\nAccountability – holding leaders responsible for outcome\nCommercial Awareness – understanding contract revenue driver\nConsistency – ensuring reliable delivery standards across the division\n\nThese behaviours form part of probation and promotion assessments.\n\nDivisional Managers are also expected to consistently demonstrate our 6 DNA values:\n\nDriven\nHow much do you want to achieve your goals?\n\nDisciplined\nConsistently performing the small actions required to achieve your goals.\n\nCompetitive\nSelf-motivated and driven to continually achieve your best.\n\nPositive\nMaintaining a solutions-focused attitude.\n\nResilient\nBouncing back quickly from setbacks.\n\nCommitted\nShowing dedication to achieving your goals and contributing to team success.\n\nAt Divisional Manager level these values are demonstrated through leadership at scale, ownership of performance and consistent delivery of results across multiple teams.\n\n', E'2026-04-17T10:04:50.335298'),
  (53, 2, E'Associate Director Perm', 13, E'Associate Director Delivery – Permanent\n\nPurpose Of The Role\n\nThe Associate Director is responsible for defining, leading and optimising the delivery function at a strategic level, ensuring it consistently supports business growth, client success and revenue performance.\n\nAssociate Directors operate as senior leaders within the business, aligning delivery capability to commercial objectives, shaping structure, standards and performance across the organisation.\n\nRole Responsibilities\n\nStrategic Ownershi\n• Take ownership of the delivery function strategy and performanc\n• Ensure delivery capability aligns with business growth plans and market deman\n• Define and evolve delivery structure to support scalability and performance\n\nLeadership & Directio\n• Lead and develop Divisional Managers and Team Leader\n• Set clear direction, priorities and expectations across the delivery functio\n• Ensure leadership consistency and accountability at all levels\n\nPerformance & Commercial Alignmen\n• Ensure delivery performance supports overall revenue and business objective\n• Monitor and improve conversion, output and efficiency across the functio\n• Identify opportunities to improve performance and commercial impact\n\nCapability & Structur\n• Build and maintain a high-performing delivery functio\n• Ensure clear standards, processes and expectations are embedde\n• Drive continuous improvement in capability, quality and consistency\n\nPipeline & Forecastin\n• Maintain visibility of delivery performance across the busines\n• Ensure pipeline strength supports current and future deman\n• Contribute to forecasting and business planning\n\nCross-Functional Collaboratio\n• Work closely with senior leadership to align delivery with sales strateg\n• Ensure delivery supports client development and retentio\n• Contribute to wider business decisions and strategy\n\nWhat Success Looks Like – How The Role Is Measured\n\nBusiness Impac\n• Delivery function contributing consistently to revenue performanc\n• Strong alignment between delivery output and business objective\n• Improved conversion, efficiency and output at scale\n\nLeadership Effectivenes\n• Strong leadership capability across Divisional Managers and Team Leader\n• High levels of accountability and performance across the functio\n• Consistent leadership standards across teams\n\nPerformance & Consistenc\n• Reliable delivery performance across all division\n• Strong pipeline coverage and predictable outpu\n• Consistent standards across the organisation\n\nCapability & Growt\n• Improvement in delivery capability and team performanc\n• Scalable and sustainable delivery structur\n• Continuous improvement in quality and standards\n\nCustomer Experienc\n• High-quality candidate experience across the busines\n• Strong reputation for delivery excellence\n\nProfessional Standard\n• Accurate reporting and visibility of performanc\n• Strong governance, organisation and accountability\n\nBehaviours & Values Expected In This Role\n\nAssociate Directors are expected to demonstrate:\n\nStrategic Leadership – shaping direction and performance of the delivery functio\nCommercial Ownership – aligning delivery to revenue and business outcome\nAccountability – holding leaders and teams responsible for performanc\nInfluence – impacting business decisions and outcomes beyond deliver\nConsistency – ensuring standards and performance at scale\n\nThese behaviours form part of probation and promotion assessments.\n\nAssociate Directors are also expected to consistently demonstrate our 6 DNA values:\n\nDriven\nHow much do you want to achieve your goals?\n\nDisciplined\nConsistently performing the small actions required to achieve your goals.\n\nCompetitive\nSelf-motivated and driven to continually achieve your best.\n\nPositive\nMaintaining a solutions-focused attitude.\n\nResilient\nBouncing back quickly from setbacks.\n\nCommitted\nShowing dedication to achieving your goals and contributing to overall business success.\n\nAt Associate Director level these values are demonstrated through strategic leadership, ownership of business outcomes and consistent delivery of performance at scale.\n\n', E'2026-04-17T10:04:50.335298'),
  (54, 2, E'Associate Director Contract', 14, E'Associate Director – Delivery Contract\n\nPurpose Of The Role\n\nThe Associate Director is responsible for defining, leading and optimising the contract delivery function at a strategic level, ensuring it consistently supports contract revenue growth, client success and business performance.\n\nAssociate Directors operate as senior leaders, aligning contractor delivery capability to commercial objectives and shaping the structure, standards and performance of the function.\n\nRole Responsibilities\n\nStrategic Ownershi\n• Take ownership of contract delivery strategy and performanc\n• Ensure contractor delivery capability aligns with business growth and market deman\n• Define and evolve delivery structure to support scalability and contract revenue\n\nLeadership & Directio\n• Lead and develop Divisional Managers and Team Leader\n• Set clear direction and expectations across the contract delivery functio\n• Ensure leadership consistency and accountability\n\nPerformance & Commercial Alignmen\n• Ensure contract delivery supports revenue growth and business objective\n• Monitor and improve conversion, pipeline strength and contractor outpu\n• Identify opportunities to improve performance and commercial impact\n\nCapability & Structur\n• Build and maintain a high-performing contract delivery functio\n• Ensure strong standards across contractor quality, pipeline management and complianc\n• Drive continuous improvement in capability and consistency\n\nPipeline & Forecastin\n• Maintain visibility of contractor pipelines across the busines\n• Ensure pipeline strength supports current and future deman\n• Contribute to contract revenue forecasting and planning\n\nCross-Functional Collaboratio\n• Work closely with senior leadership and sales team\n• Ensure delivery supports client development and retentio\n• Contribute to wider business strategy\n\nWhat Success Looks Like – How The Role Is Measured\n\nBusiness Impac\n• Contract delivery function contributing to revenue growt\n• Strong alignment between delivery output and business objective\n• Improved conversion, efficiency and output at scale\n\nLeadership Effectivenes\n• Strong leadership capability across Divisional Managers and Team Leader\n• High accountability and performance across the function\n\nPerformance & Consistenc\n• Reliable contractor delivery performance across division\n• Strong pipeline coverage and predictable output\n\nCapability & Growt\n• Improvement in contract delivery capabilit\n• Scalable and sustainable structure\n\nCustomer Experienc\n• High-quality contractor experience across the business\n\nProfessional Standard\n• Accurate reporting, compliance and governanc\n• Strong organisation and accountability\n\nBehaviours & Values Expected In This Role\n\nAssociate Directors are expected to demonstrate:\n\nStrategic Leadership – shaping direction of the contract delivery functio\nCommercial Ownership – aligning delivery to contract revenue outcome\nAccountability – holding leaders responsible for performanc\nInfluence – impacting business decisions and strateg\nConsistency – ensuring standards at scale\n\nThese behaviours form part of probation and promotion assessments.\n\nAssociate Directors are also expected to consistently demonstrate our 6 DNA values:\n\nDriven\nHow much do you want to achieve your goals?\n\nDisciplined\nConsistently performing the small actions required to achieve your goals.\n\nCompetitive\nSelf-motivated and driven to continually achieve your best.\n\nPositive\nMaintaining a solutions-focused attitude.\n\nResilient\nBouncing back quickly from setbacks.\n\nCommitted\nShowing dedication to achieving your goals and contributing to overall business success.\n\nAt Associate Director level these values are demonstrated through strategic leadership, ownership of business outcomes and consistent delivery of performance at scale.\n\n', E'2026-04-17T10:04:50.335298')
